This product statically links third-party software whose licenses require
attribution and, in the case of LGPL-2.1 components, the ability for the
end user to relink against a modified version of the library. Source for
those components is pinned in this repository's build system; the
`zig build` recipe rebuilds the binary from source. See
THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md for the full list, pinned versions, license texts,
and links to upstream source.

Statically-linked third-party components:

  - libcrun (https://github.com/containers/crun, files under `src/libcrun/`)
    LGPL-2.1-or-later

  - libseccomp (https://github.com/seccomp/libseccomp)
    LGPL-2.1-only

  - libcap (https://sites.google.com/site/fullycapable/)
    BSD-3-Clause (selected from the BSD/GPL-2.0 dual-license offer)

  - yajl (https://github.com/lloyd/yajl) -- or libcrun's embedded copy
    ISC

  - musl libc (Zig-bundled) (https://musl.libc.org/)
    MIT

`libsystemd` and `libcriu` are explicitly disabled at libcrun configure
time. The released rind binary contains no GPL-only components.
